{
  "id": "binary-tree-level-order-traversal",
  "title": "Binary Tree Level Order Traversal",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["tree", "bfs"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given the `root` of a binary tree, list its values **level by level**. Return a list with one inner list per depth, starting from the root; inside each level, values appear from left to right.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nroot = [3, 9, 20, null, null, 15, 7]\n→ [[3], [9, 20], [15, 7]]\n```\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nroot = [1]\n→ [[1]]\n```\n\n**Example 3**\n\n```\nroot = []\n→ []\n```",
  "constraints": ["0 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 2000", "-1000 ≤ Node.val ≤ 1000"],
  "hints": ["A first-in, first-out queue visits nodes in exactly the order you need.", "How can you tell where one level stops and the next one begins while the queue keeps growing?"],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "levelOrder",
    "params": [{ "name": "root", "type": "TreeNode" }],
    "returns": "int[][]"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
  "tests": [
    { "input": [[3,9,20,null,null,15,7]], "expected": [[3],[9,20],[15,7]] },
    { "input": [[1]], "expected": [[1]] },
    { "input": [[]], "expected": [] },
    { "input": [[1,2,3,4,5,6,7]], "expected": [[1],[2,3],[4,5,6,7]], "hidden": true },
    { "input": [[1,2,null,3,null,4,null,5]], "expected": [[1],[2],[3],[4],[5]], "hidden": true },
    { "input": [[1,null,2,null,3]], "expected": [[1],[2],[3]], "hidden": true },
    { "input": [[1,2,3,null,4,null,5]], "expected": [[1],[2,3],[4,5]], "hidden": true },
    { "input": [[0,0,0,0,null,null,0]], "expected": [[0],[0,0],[0,0]], "hidden": true },
